IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gaa-dates`

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) -- the rules, seat-neutral where the text is, worded for the
-- represented person where a question needs a seat.
--
-- Focus: guardians and administrators for adults without decision-making capacity, including the management of a
-- compensation award. Parts 1, 3 and 4 (definitions, capacity, guardianship, administration and supportive orders),
-- the rehearing and reassessment time limits of Part 7, and Part 9's remuneration, court money (s 179), compensation
-- (ss 181-186) and offences (ss 188-192). Out: Part 2 (the Public Advocate's office), Part 5 (missing persons), Part 6
-- (special medical procedures), Part 8 (interstate orders), Part 10 (transitional). Reasons in NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions (rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words ("means",
-- "if", "only if", "unless", "until", a flat negative); NOTHING, or a "not covered" constructor, where the text is
-- silent or a grant is limited by its own wording and the case falls outside it. Each such site is tagged NOTHING-kind
-- and each case-by-case reading is a fork line in NOTES.md (F1-F13).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Guardianship
-- and Administration Act 2019, Version No. 010 (15 April 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria;
-- published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except
-- in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guardianship and Administration Act 2019: the rules`

§§ `Part 1 -- definitions and decision-making capacity`

-- s 3(1): "disability, in relation to a person, means neurological impairment, intellectual impairment, mental
-- disorder, brain injury, physical disability or dementia". A "means" definition: outside the list, JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `Kind of impairment` IS ONE OF
    `a neurological impairment`
    `an intellectual impairment`
    `a mental disorder`
    `a brain injury`
    `a physical disability`
    `dementia`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the impairment` IS A `Kind of impairment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- I have a disability` `the impairment` IF
    NOT (`the impairment` EQUALS `none of these`)

-- s 5(1): a person has decision-making capacity for a matter "if the person is able" to (a) understand the relevant
-- information and the effect of the decision, (b) retain it, (c) use or weigh it, (d) communicate the decision. (2):
-- "presumed to have decision-making capacity unless there is evidence to the contrary". (3): understanding an
-- explanation given in a way appropriate to the person counts. (4)(c), (d): capacity "should not be assumed" absent on
-- the basis of appearance or merely because a decision is unwise; (e): a person has capacity "if it is possible for the
-- person to make the decision with practicable and appropriate support". Whether each limb is met is a judgment for
-- whoever assesses (s 6); the limbs are inputs, each asked with any practicable and appropriate support.
-- Fork F1: doubt resting only on appearance or an unwise decision is taken not to be "evidence to the contrary".
DECLARE `Whether I have decision-making capacity` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am presumed to have it, as there is no evidence to the contrary (s 5(2))`
    `yes: I can understand, retain, use or weigh, and communicate the decision, with any practicable and appropriate support (s 5(1), (3), (4)(e))`
    `no: I do not have it for this matter, though I may for others, and it may be temporary (s 5(1), (4)(a), (b))`

GIVEN `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the doubt rests only on my appearance or an unwise decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can understand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can retain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can use or weigh` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can communicate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether I have decision-making capacity`
`s 5 -- my decision-making capacity` `there is evidence to the contrary` `the doubt rests only on my appearance or an unwise decision` `I can understand` `I can retain` `I can use or weigh` `I can communicate` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`) OR `the doubt rests only on my appearance or an unwise decision`
    THEN `yes: I am presumed to have it, as there is no evidence to the contrary (s 5(2))`
    ELSE IF `I can understand` AND `I can retain` AND `I can use or weigh` AND `I can communicate`
         THEN `yes: I can understand, retain, use or weigh, and communicate the decision, with any practicable and appropriate support (s 5(1), (3), (4)(e))`
         ELSE `no: I do not have it for this matter, though I may for others, and it may be temporary (s 5(1), (4)(a), (b))`

-- s 3(1): "nearest relative means the relative first listed in the definition of relative who is of or over 18 years
-- of age, the elder or eldest of 2 or more relatives described in any paragraph being preferred". The list: (a) spouse
-- or domestic partner; (b) child; (c) parent; (d) step-parent; (e) sibling (including one adopted by a parent, s 3(3));
-- (f) step-sibling; (g) grandparent; (h) grandchild; (i) uncle or aunt; (j) nephew or niece. Within a paragraph the
-- eldest is preferred; the answer names the paragraph.
DECLARE `My nearest relative` IS ONE OF
    `my spouse or domestic partner (s 3, relative (a))`
    `my eldest adult child (s 3, relative (b))`
    `my elder or eldest parent (s 3, relative (c))`
    `my elder or eldest step-parent (s 3, relative (d))`
    `my eldest adult sibling (s 3, relative (e))`
    `my eldest adult step-sibling (s 3, relative (f))`
    `my eldest grandparent (s 3, relative (g))`
    `my eldest adult grandchild (s 3, relative (h))`
    `my eldest uncle or aunt (s 3, relative (i))`
    `my eldest adult nephew or niece (s 3, relative (j))`
    `I have no relative aged 18 or over, so no nearest relative`

GIVEN `a spouse or domestic partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult step-parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult sibling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult step-sibling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult grandparent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult grandchild` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult uncle or aunt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult nephew or niece` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My nearest relative`
`s 3 -- my nearest relative` `a spouse or domestic partner` `an adult child` `an adult parent` `an adult step-parent` `an adult sibling` `an adult step-sibling` `an adult grandparent` `an adult grandchild` `an adult uncle or aunt` `an adult nephew or niece` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a spouse or domestic partner` THEN `my spouse or domestic partner (s 3, relative (a))`
        IF `an adult child` THEN `my eldest adult child (s 3, relative (b))`
        IF `an adult parent` THEN `my elder or eldest parent (s 3, relative (c))`
        IF `an adult step-parent` THEN `my elder or eldest step-parent (s 3, relative (d))`
        IF `an adult sibling` THEN `my eldest adult sibling (s 3, relative (e))`
        IF `an adult step-sibling` THEN `my eldest adult step-sibling (s 3, relative (f))`
        IF `an adult grandparent` THEN `my eldest grandparent (s 3, relative (g))`
        IF `an adult grandchild` THEN `my eldest adult grandchild (s 3, relative (h))`
        IF `an adult uncle or aunt` THEN `my eldest uncle or aunt (s 3, relative (i))`
        IF `an adult nephew or niece` THEN `my eldest adult nephew or niece (s 3, relative (j))`
        OTHERWISE `I have no relative aged 18 or over, so no nearest relative`

§§ `Parts 3 and 4 -- applications and the making of orders`

DECLARE `Kind of order` IS ONE OF
    `a guardianship order`
    `an administration order`
    `a supportive guardianship order`
    `a supportive administration order`

GIVEN `the order` IS A `Kind of order`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is about money or property` `the order` IF
    `the order` EQUALS `an administration order` OR `the order` EQUALS `a supportive administration order`

-- ss 22, 23(1), 79, 80(1): "A person may apply to VCAT for a [guardianship / administration / supportive guardianship /
-- supportive administration] order that appoints a [guardian ...] for a person with a disability who is (a) of or over
-- 18 years of age; or (b) under 18 years of age but the order takes effect on that person attaining 18 years of age."
-- ss 23(2), 80(2): if the person "does not reside in Victoria but the person's property is partly or wholly in
-- Victoria", the application may be made "in relation to that part of the property that is in Victoria". A grant
-- limited in its own wording: outside it, not covered (NOTHING-kind). Fork F3: a non-resident with no property in
-- Victoria is outside the grant for the money orders; residence is not mentioned for the personal orders.
DECLARE `Whether an application can be made for me` IS ONE OF
    `yes: anyone may apply to VCAT for this order for me (ss 22, 23, 79, 80)`
    `yes, but only for my property that is in Victoria (ss 23(2), 80(2))`
    `not covered: the Act provides for applications only for a person with a disability (s 3)`
    `not covered: I am under 18 and the order would not take effect only when I turn 18`
    `not covered: I do not live in Victoria and have no property here`

GIVEN `the order` IS A `Kind of order`
      `the impairment` IS A `Kind of impairment`
      `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `the order would take effect when I turn 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I live in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have property in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether an application can be made for me`
`ss 22, 23, 79, 80 -- whether an application can be made for me` `the order` `the impairment` `my age` `the order would take effect when I turn 18` `I live in Victoria` `I have property in Victoria` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 3 -- I have a disability` `the impairment`)
            THEN `not covered: the Act provides for applications only for a person with a disability (s 3)` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF `my age` LESS THAN 18 AND (NOT `the order would take effect when I turn 18`)
            THEN `not covered: I am under 18 and the order would not take effect only when I turn 18` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF (`the order is about money or property` `the order`) AND (NOT `I live in Victoria`)
            THEN IF `I have property in Victoria`
                 THEN `yes, but only for my property that is in Victoria (ss 23(2), 80(2))`
                 ELSE `not covered: I do not live in Victoria and have no property here` -- NOTHING-kind
        OTHERWISE `yes: anyone may apply to VCAT for this order for me (ss 22, 23, 79, 80)`

-- s 30(2): "VCAT may only make a guardianship order or an administration order ... if satisfied that (a) because of
-- the proposed represented person's disability, the person does not have decision-making capacity in relation to" the
-- matter; "(b) the proposed represented person is in need of a guardian or administrator" (s 31 factors); "(c) the
-- ... order ... will promote the proposed represented person's personal and social wellbeing; and (d) in the case of
-- an application for an administration order for a proposed represented person who does not reside in Victoria, State
-- Trustees has not been authorised under section 12 of the State Trustees (State Owned Company) Act 1994" over the
-- property. "Only if": JUST FALSE when a limb fails. VCAT's satisfaction on each limb is an input.
DECLARE `Kind of appointment` IS ONE OF `a guardian`, `an administrator`

GIVEN `the appointment` IS A `Kind of appointment`
      `VCAT is satisfied I lack capacity for the matter because of my disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied I need a guardian or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied the order will promote my wellbeing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I live in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `State Trustees is authorised under s 12 over the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(2) -- VCAT may appoint a guardian or administrator for me` `the appointment` `VCAT is satisfied I lack capacity for the matter because of my disability` `VCAT is satisfied I need a guardian or administrator` `VCAT is satisfied the order will promote my wellbeing` `I live in Victoria` `State Trustees is authorised under s 12 over the property` MEANS
    IF `VCAT is satisfied I lack capacity for the matter because of my disability`
       AND `VCAT is satisfied I need a guardian or administrator`
       AND `VCAT is satisfied the order will promote my wellbeing`
       AND (NOT (`the appointment` EQUALS `an administrator` AND (NOT `I live in Victoria`) AND `State Trustees is authorised under s 12 over the property`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 87(2): "VCAT may only make an order appointing a supportive guardian or a supportive administrator ... if VCAT is
-- satisfied that (a) the person consents to VCAT making the order; and (b) if the person is given practicable and
-- appropriate support, the person will have decision-making capacity in relation to the ... matter ...; and (c) the
-- ... order ... will promote the person's personal and social wellbeing." "Only if": JUST FALSE when a limb fails.
GIVEN `I consent to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied I will have capacity with support` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied the order will promote my wellbeing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(2) -- VCAT may appoint a supportive guardian or administrator for me` `I consent to the order` `VCAT is satisfied I will have capacity with support` `VCAT is satisfied the order will promote my wellbeing` MEANS
    IF `I consent to the order` AND `VCAT is satisfied I will have capacity with support` AND `VCAT is satisfied the order will promote my wellbeing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 32(1): VCAT may appoint as a guardian "any individual who is of or over the age of 18 years and who consents to act
-- as guardian if VCAT is satisfied that the individual (a) will act in accordance with the duties ...; (b) is not in a
-- position where the individual's interests conflict, or may conflict, with the interests of the proposed represented
-- person; and (c) is a suitable person". (2): an administrator may be "any person (individual or body corporate)",
-- an individual being 18 or over, who consents, with (a)-(c) and "(d) has sufficient expertise to make decisions about
-- any financial matter". s 88(1): a supportive guardian or administrator is "any individual who is of or over 18 years
-- of age and who consents", if VCAT is satisfied of the s 94 duties and suitability. The "if VCAT is satisfied" limbs:
-- JUST FALSE when one fails. Who may be appointed at all (an individual of 18 or over; a body corporate only as
-- administrator): a grant limited in its own wording, so NOTHING outside it (fork F4). s 32(5): VCAT must not assume a
-- relative is conflicted or unsuitable merely for being a relative or disagreeing with another relative.
DECLARE `Kind of appointee` IS ONE OF `an individual`, `a body corporate`

GIVEN `the order` IS A `Kind of order`
      `the appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee`
      `their age` IS A NUMBER
      `they consent to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied they will act in accordance with the duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied they have no conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied they are suitable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied they have sufficient financial expertise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 32, 88 -- this person may be appointed for me` `the order` `the appointee` `their age` `they consent to act` `VCAT is satisfied they will act in accordance with the duties` `VCAT is satisfied they have no conflict of interest` `VCAT is satisfied they are suitable` `VCAT is satisfied they have sufficient financial expertise` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appointee` EQUALS `a body corporate` AND (NOT (`the order` EQUALS `an administration order`))
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: ss 32(1), 88(1) provide for individuals only
        IF `the appointee` EQUALS `an individual` AND `their age` LESS THAN 18
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: ss 32, 88 provide for individuals of 18 or over only
        IF NOT `they consent to act`
            THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the order` EQUALS `a guardianship order`
            THEN JUST (`VCAT is satisfied they will act in accordance with the duties` AND `VCAT is satisfied they have no conflict of interest` AND `VCAT is satisfied they are suitable`)
        IF `the order` EQUALS `an administration order`
            THEN JUST (`VCAT is satisfied they will act in accordance with the duties` AND `VCAT is satisfied they have no conflict of interest` AND `VCAT is satisfied they are suitable` AND `VCAT is satisfied they have sufficient financial expertise`)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`VCAT is satisfied they will act in accordance with the duties` AND `VCAT is satisfied they are suitable`)

-- s 36(3): an urgent order "(a) remains in force for the period specified in the order, being a period not exceeding
-- 21 days; and (b) may be renewed once for a further period not exceeding 21 days." Fork F5: the period runs from the
-- day after the order is made, so the last day in force is that many days after the day of making. A period over 21
-- days is outside what s 36 allows: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the day it was made` IS A DATE
      `the days it specifies` IS A NUMBER
      `it was renewed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days of the renewal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 36(3) -- the last day my urgent order is in force` `the day it was made` `the days it specifies` `it was renewed` `the days of the renewal` MEANS
    IF `the days it specifies` GREATER THAN 21 OR (`it was renewed` AND `the days of the renewal` GREATER THAN 21)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 36(3) does not provide for a period over 21 days
    ELSE IF `it was renewed`
         THEN JUST (`the date` (`the days it specifies` PLUS `the days of the renewal`) `days after` `the day it was made`)
         ELSE JUST (`the date` `the days it specifies` `days after` `the day it was made`)

§§ `Deadlines run as regulative rules`

-- The parties and steps of the five deadline rules below. Day 0 is the day the period runs from; WITHIN n allows the
-- step on day n ("within n days after the day ...": the day itself excluded, the n-th day after it the last day).
DECLARE `Deadline party` IS ONE OF `VCAT`, `me, or the person applying for me`

DECLARE `Deadline step` IS ONE OF
    `start hearing the application`
    `hold the hearing after the urgent order`
    `apply for a rehearing, or for leave to apply`
    `request in writing a hearing of the reassessment`
    `apply for an order for compensation`

-- s 28 (and s 85 for supportive orders): "VCAT must commence to hear an application made under this Division within
-- 30 days after the day on which the application is received by VCAT unless" VCAT or the principal registrar requires
-- a compulsory conference or refers the proceeding for mediation.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
`s 28 -- VCAT must start hearing within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY `VCAT`
    MUST `start hearing the application`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `VCAT` BECAUSE "VCAT did not commence to hear the application within 30 days after the day it was received (s 28)"

-- s 37: "As soon as practicable after making a guardianship order or an administration order that is an urgent order
-- (but within 42 days after making such an order) VCAT must hold a hearing to determine whether a guardianship order
-- or an administration order ... that is not an urgent order should be made."
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
`s 37 -- VCAT must hold a hearing within 42 days of an urgent order` MEANS
    PARTY `VCAT`
    MUST `hold the hearing after the urgent order`
    WITHIN 42
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `VCAT` BECAUSE "VCAT did not hold the hearing within 42 days after making the urgent order (s 37)"

-- s 152(1): an application for a rehearing, or for leave, "must be made within 28 days after the day on which VCAT
-- makes the order on the rehearing or the reassessment" (finding 1: read as the order to be reheard). (2): if VCAT gave
-- oral reasons and a party then requested written reasons under s 117 of the VCAT Act, "the day on which the written
-- reasons are given to the party is taken to be the day on which the order is made". No extension power in this Act.
-- The breach is the loss of the right, not a wrong.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
`s 152 -- apply for a rehearing within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `me, or the person applying for me`
    DO `apply for a rehearing, or for leave to apply`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `me, or the person applying for me` BECAUSE "no application for a rehearing or for leave within 28 days after the day of the order (s 152)"

-- s 164(4): where VCAT does not propose to change the order and intends to reassess on the papers, it may notify that
-- a party or person "has 14 days after the date of the notice to request, in writing, a hearing". (5): a request
-- "within 14 days after the date of the notice" means VCAT must give at least 7 days' notice of a hearing; (6): if none
-- is made, "VCAT is not required to hold a hearing of the reassessment".
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
`s 164 -- request a reassessment hearing within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `me, or the person applying for me`
    DO `request in writing a hearing of the reassessment`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `me, or the person applying for me` BECAUSE "no written request for a hearing within 14 days after the date of the notice; VCAT need not hold a hearing (s 164(6))"

-- s 184(1): an application for compensation under s 181 "must be made (a) if the represented person ... has died,
-- within 6 months after that death; or (b) if the guardian or administrator has died, within 6 months after that
-- death; or (c) if both ... have died, within 6 months after the first death." (2): "The Supreme Court or VCAT may
-- extend the time". The number of days allowed is worked from the dates (6 months, or the extended day).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
`s 184 -- apply for compensation within the time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `me, or the person applying for me`
    DO `apply for an order for compensation`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `me, or the person applying for me` BECAUSE "no application for compensation within 6 months after the death, or the extended time (s 184)"

-- Runs a deadline rule by EVALTRACE: is the step, taken on day t, in time?
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
      `the step` IS A `Deadline step`
      `the party` IS A `Deadline party`
      t IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `under` `the rule` `the step` `by` `the party` `on day` t `is in time` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL t), (EVENT `the party` `the step` t))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where the step stands` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done yet, and still in time`
    `not done, and the time has passed`
    `done, but out of time`
    `no time limit under this provision`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
      `the party` IS A `Deadline party`
      `the step` IS A `Deadline step`
      `the day time runs from` IS A DATE
      `it has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`where the step stands under` `the rule` `the party` `the step` `the day time runs from` `it has been done` `the day it was done` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has been done`
    THEN IF `under` `the rule` `the step` `by` `the party` `on day` (`the days from` `the day time runs from` `to` `the day it was done`) `is in time`
         THEN `done in time`
         ELSE `done, but out of time`
    ELSE IF `under` `the rule` `the step` `by` `the party` `on day` (`the days from` `the day time runs from` `to` `today`) `is in time`
         THEN `not done yet, and still in time`
         ELSE `not done, and the time has passed`

GIVEN `there is a compulsory conference or mediation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day VCAT received the application` IS A DATE
      `the hearing has started` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it started` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`s 28 -- where the start of my hearing stands` `there is a compulsory conference or mediation` `the day VCAT received the application` `the hearing has started` `the day it started` `today` MEANS
    IF `there is a compulsory conference or mediation`
    THEN `no time limit under this provision`
    ELSE `where the step stands under` `s 28 -- VCAT must start hearing within 30 days` `VCAT` `start hearing the application` `the day VCAT received the application` `the hearing has started` `the day it started` `today`

GIVEN `the day the urgent order was made` IS A DATE
      `the hearing has been held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was held` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`s 37 -- where the hearing after my urgent order stands` `the day the urgent order was made` `the hearing has been held` `the day it was held` `today` MEANS
    `where the step stands under` `s 37 -- VCAT must hold a hearing within 42 days of an urgent order` `VCAT` `hold the hearing after the urgent order` `the day the urgent order was made` `the hearing has been held` `the day it was held` `today`

GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `written reasons were requested after oral reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the written reasons were given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 152(2) -- the day of the order` `the day the order was made` `written reasons were requested after oral reasons` `the day the written reasons were given` MEANS
    IF `written reasons were requested after oral reasons`
    THEN `the day the written reasons were given`
    ELSE `the day the order was made`

GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`s 152 -- where my rehearing application stands` `the day of the order` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today` MEANS
    `where the step stands under` `s 152 -- apply for a rehearing within 28 days` `me, or the person applying for me` `apply for a rehearing, or for leave to apply` `the day of the order` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today`

GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE
      `I have requested a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I requested it` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`s 164 -- where my request for a reassessment hearing stands` `the date of the notice` `I have requested a hearing` `the day I requested it` `today` MEANS
    `where the step stands under` `s 164 -- request a reassessment hearing within 14 days` `me, or the person applying for me` `request in writing a hearing of the reassessment` `the date of the notice` `I have requested a hearing` `the day I requested it` `today`

§§ `Part 7 -- rehearings and reassessments`

-- s 150(1): "The Public Advocate and any person who was a party to an application in relation to which VCAT made an
-- order under this Act (other than an urgent order appointing a guardian or an administrator) may apply to VCAT for a
-- rehearing". (2): a person entitled to notice who was not a party may, "if VCAT gives leave". s 151: after a
-- reassessment "conducted on VCAT's own initiative", a party or a person entitled to notice may, with leave. s 153: "A
-- person cannot apply for a rehearing of (a) an application in relation to which an order was made by VCAT constituted
-- by the President ...; (b) an application for a rehearing; (c), (d) an application for leave". The proposed
-- represented person is always a party (s 25(b); s 161(b) for reassessments).
-- Fork F6: "(other than an urgent order ...)" is taken as outside the grant (not covered), not as a flat no.
-- Fork F7: a reassessment on someone's application (s 159(3)) is taken as "an application" within s 150.
DECLARE `My role in the proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `I was a party`
    `I was entitled to notice but was not a party`
    `neither`

DECLARE `The order to be reheard` IS ONE OF
    `an order on an application`
    `an urgent order appointing a guardian or administrator`
    `an order on a reassessment VCAT conducted on its own initiative`
    `an order on a reassessment someone applied for`
    `an order on an application for a rehearing or for leave`

DECLARE `Whether I can apply for a rehearing` IS ONE OF
    `yes, as a party (s 150(1))`
    `yes, if VCAT gives leave (s 150(2))`
    `yes, if VCAT gives leave (s 151)`
    `no: a rehearing cannot be sought of this (s 153)`
    `not covered: s 150 excludes urgent orders appointing a guardian or administrator`
    `not covered: the Act gives the right only to a party or a person entitled to notice`

GIVEN `my role` IS A `My role in the proceeding`
      `the order` IS A `The order to be reheard`
      `VCAT was constituted by the President` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether I can apply for a rehearing`
`ss 150, 151, 153 -- whether I can apply for a rehearing` `my role` `the order` `VCAT was constituted by the President` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order` EQUALS `an order on an application for a rehearing or for leave`
            THEN `no: a rehearing cannot be sought of this (s 153)`
        IF `VCAT was constituted by the President` AND (NOT (`the order` EQUALS `an order on a reassessment VCAT conducted on its own initiative`))
            THEN `no: a rehearing cannot be sought of this (s 153)`
        IF `the order` EQUALS `an urgent order appointing a guardian or administrator`
            THEN `not covered: s 150 excludes urgent orders appointing a guardian or administrator` -- NOTHING-kind (fork F6)
        IF `my role` EQUALS `neither`
            THEN `not covered: the Act gives the right only to a party or a person entitled to notice` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF `the order` EQUALS `an order on a reassessment VCAT conducted on its own initiative`
            THEN `yes, if VCAT gives leave (s 151)`
        IF `my role` EQUALS `I was a party`
            THEN `yes, as a party (s 150(1))`
        OTHERWISE `yes, if VCAT gives leave (s 150(2))`

-- s 159(2): "VCAT must conduct a reassessment of an order (a) within 12 months after making the order, unless VCAT
-- orders otherwise; and (b) in any case, at least once within each 3 year period after making the order, unless VCAT
-- orders otherwise." Read literally (fork F8, finding 3): fixed 3-year periods counted from the making of the order,
-- not rolling from the last reassessment. Until the first reassessment the 12-month day governs. After it, the period
-- holding the latest reassessment is satisfied and the next one must hold a reassessment by its last day.
GIVEN `the latest reassessment` IS A DATE
      `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 159 -- the 3-year period holding` `the latest reassessment` `of an order made on` `the day the order was made` MEANS
    IF `the rough period` GREATER THAN 0 AND (DATE_SERIAL (`the date` (3 TIMES `the rough period`) `years after` `the day the order was made`) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `the latest reassessment`)
    THEN `the rough period` MINUS 1
    ELSE `the rough period`
    WHERE
        `the rough period` MEANS FLOOR ((`the whole years from` `the day the order was made` `to` `the latest reassessment`) DIVIDED BY 3)

GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `VCAT has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a reassessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the latest reassessment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 159(2) -- the last day for VCAT's next reassessment of my order` `the day the order was made` `VCAT has ordered otherwise` `there has been a reassessment` `the latest reassessment` MEANS
    IF `VCAT has ordered otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: the timing is then whatever VCAT ordered
    ELSE IF NOT `there has been a reassessment`
         THEN JUST (`the date` 12 `months after` `the day the order was made`)
         ELSE JUST (`the date` (3 TIMES ((`s 159 -- the 3-year period holding` `the latest reassessment` `of an order made on` `the day the order was made`) PLUS 2)) `years after` `the day the order was made`)

§§ `Part 3 Divisions 3 and 6 -- what my guardian or administrator can do`

-- ss 39 and 53: "Despite anything to the contrary in this Division, a guardianship [administration] order does not
-- confer on the person appointed ... the power (a) to make or revoke a will ...; (b) to make or revoke an enduring power
-- of attorney ...; (c) to vote ...; (d) to consent to the entering into, or dissolving of, a marriage ... or a sexual
-- relationship ...; (e) to make or give effect to a decision about (i) the care and wellbeing of a child of the
-- represented person; or (ii) the adoption of a child ...; (f) ... a surrogacy arrangement ...; (g) ... a substitute
-- parentage order ...; (h) to manage the estate of the represented person on the death of the represented person; or
-- (i) to consent to an unlawful act." A flat negative: JUST FALSE. Anything else depends on the order: NOTHING.
DECLARE `Act done for me` IS ONE OF
    `make or revoke my will`
    `make or revoke my enduring power of attorney`
    `vote for me in an election or referendum`
    `consent to my marriage, divorce or a sexual relationship`
    `decide about the care of my child, or the adoption of my child`
    `enter into a surrogacy arrangement for me`
    `consent to making or discharging a substitute parentage order for me`
    `manage my estate after my death`
    `consent to an unlawful act`
    `something else`

GIVEN `the act` IS AN `Act done for me`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 39, 53 -- my guardian or administrator can do this for me` `the act` MEANS
    IF `the act` EQUALS `something else`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: it depends on the matters and powers the order specifies (ss 34, 38, 46)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 46(1): an administration order confers "(a) a power to make decisions about the financial matters ... specified in
-- the order; ... (e) any other power that is specified in the order". "financial matter" includes, by example (s 3),
-- "(d) receiving and recovering money payable to the person". s 52: VCAT may specify "(a) the power to collect,
-- receive and recover ... (iii) any compensation or damages for injury to the estate or person of the represented
-- person". s 54: "An administration order lapses on the death of the represented person". s 69(2): "An administrator
-- may exercise all or any of the powers ... until the administrator knows that the represented person has ceased to
-- be a represented person or has died." Fork F9 (finding 4): s 69(2) is taken to keep the powers until the
-- administrator knows of the death, despite s 54; the "until" bar answers JUST FALSE once the administrator knows.
-- Without a specified s 52(a) power or a specified matter covering it: NOTHING (the order does not reach it).
DECLARE `Whether my administration order has ended` IS ONE OF
    `it is in force`
    `I have died`
    `I have ceased to be a represented person`

GIVEN `the state of the order` IS A `Whether my administration order has ended`
      `my administrator knows it has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order specifies the s 52(a) power to collect compensation or damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order specifies a financial matter covering receiving money payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 46, 52, 54, 69 -- my administrator may collect my compensation or damages` `the state of the order` `my administrator knows it has ended` `the order specifies the s 52(a) power to collect compensation or damages` `the order specifies a financial matter covering receiving money payable to me` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the state of the order` EQUALS `it is in force`)) AND `my administrator knows it has ended`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the order specifies the s 52(a) power to collect compensation or damages` OR `the order specifies a financial matter covering receiving money payable to me`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: the order does not give the power

-- s 38(1)(c): a guardianship order confers "the power to undertake legal proceedings under section 40, if specified in
-- the order"; s 40(1): VCAT may specify that power "if the action or other legal proceeding is in relation to a
-- personal matter specified in the order". s 51(1): the same for an administrator and "a financial matter specified in
-- the order"; "legal matter" (s 3) includes "settling a claim before or after a legal proceeding ... starts", and
-- s 52(i) the power "to ... settle, adjust or compromise any demand made by or against the represented person's
-- estate". ss 40(2), 51(2): no need to be appointed litigation guardian. For a guardian "if specified" answers JUST
-- FALSE when not specified; for an administrator the s 51 power is a grant VCAT "may specify", so NOTHING when it
-- has not (fork F10).
GIVEN `the appointment` IS A `Kind of appointment`
      `the order specifies the power to bring and defend proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding relates to a matter specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 38, 40, 51 -- my guardian or administrator may bring or defend a proceeding in my name` `the appointment` `the order specifies the power to bring and defend proceedings` `the proceeding relates to a matter specified in the order` MEANS
    IF `the order specifies the power to bring and defend proceedings` AND `the proceeding relates to a matter specified in the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the appointment` EQUALS `a guardian`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (fork F10)

-- ss 40(3), 51(3): "the costs of the proceeding are to be paid out of the represented person's estate". (4): "Despite
-- subsection (3), a court or tribunal may order that a guardian [administrator] is personally liable to pay for any
-- costs ... if the guardian [administrator] was negligent or engaged in misconduct." (5): reimbursement from the
-- estate of costs incurred.
DECLARE `Who pays the costs of my proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `my estate pays them (ss 40(3), 51(3))`
    `my guardian or administrator personally, as the court or tribunal ordered for negligence or misconduct (ss 40(4), 51(4))`

GIVEN `a court or tribunal has ordered them personally liable for negligence or misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who pays the costs of my proceeding`
`ss 40, 51 -- who pays the costs of my proceeding` `a court or tribunal has ordered them personally liable for negligence or misconduct` MEANS
    IF `a court or tribunal has ordered them personally liable for negligence or misconduct`
    THEN `my guardian or administrator personally, as the court or tribunal ordered for negligence or misconduct (ss 40(4), 51(4))`
    ELSE `my estate pays them (ss 40(3), 51(3))`

-- s 47(1): "Except as provided in any order of VCAT, an administrator may make a gift of a represented person's
-- property if (a) the gift is reasonable, having regard to all the circumstances, including the represented person's
-- financial circumstances; and (b) the gift is (i) to a relative or a close friend ... and is of a seasonal nature or
-- for a special event; or (ii) of a type of donation that the represented person made when [having capacity] or ...
-- might reasonably be expected to make." (2): the gift may go to the administrator or the administrator's relatives,
-- friends or organisations. "If": JUST FALSE when it fails. A VCAT order on gifts governs instead: NOTHING.
DECLARE `Kind of gift` IS ONE OF
    `a seasonal or special-event gift to my relative or close friend`
    `a donation of a kind I made, or might reasonably be expected to make`
    `another kind of gift`

GIVEN `VCAT has made an order about gifts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift is reasonable in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift` IS A `Kind of gift`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47 -- my administrator may make this gift from my property` `VCAT has made an order about gifts` `the gift is reasonable in all the circumstances` `the gift` MEANS
    IF `VCAT has made an order about gifts`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: VCAT's order governs
    ELSE JUST (`the gift is reasonable in all the circumstances` AND (NOT (`the gift` EQUALS `another kind of gift`)))

-- s 61(4)(b): the yearly account must "include details of any gift made by the administrator of the represented
-- person's property with a total value of or over the prescribed amount (or, if an amount is not prescribed, of or over
-- $100) to (i) the administrator; or (ii) a relative or close friend of the administrator; or (iii) an organisation
-- with which the administrator has a connection." No regulations are deposited: the prescribed amount is an input, 0
-- meaning none is prescribed (finding 2: the note to s 47 says "whichever is greater"; the section governs).
DECLARE `Who received the gift` IS ONE OF
    `my administrator`
    `a relative or close friend of my administrator`
    `an organisation connected with my administrator`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Whether the gift must be detailed in the account` IS ONE OF
    `yes: its details must be in the yearly account (s 61(4)(b))`
    `not under s 61(4)(b); it is still a disbursement in the full and true account (s 61(4)(a)(ii))`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A `Who received the gift`
      `the total value` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Whether the gift must be detailed in the account`
`s 61(4)(b) -- whether the gift must be detailed in the account` `the recipient` `the total value` `the prescribed amount` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the recipient` EQUALS `someone else`)) AND `the total value` AT LEAST `the threshold`
    THEN `yes: its details must be in the yearly account (s 61(4)(b))`
    ELSE `not under s 61(4)(b); it is still a disbursement in the full and true account (s 61(4)(a)(ii))`
    WHERE
        `the threshold` MEANS IF `the prescribed amount` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the prescribed amount` ELSE 100

-- s 57(1): "Subject to section 58, an administrator must not enter into a transaction ... if the transaction is one in
-- which there is, or may be, a conflict between (a) the duty of the administrator to the represented person; and (b)
-- the interests of the administrator, or of a relative, business associate or close friend of the administrator." (2):
-- not to a s 47 gift, a s 52(n) maintenance transaction for a dependant, or a transaction "merely because" it deals with
-- property held jointly with the administrator (or a loan or guarantee for it). s 58(1): permitted "if VCAT authorises
-- the administrator at or before the time"; (2), (3): VCAT may validate a prohibited transaction, "taken to be valid
-- from the time it was entered into".
DECLARE `Conflict exception` IS ONE OF
    `no exception`
    `a gift under s 47`
    `maintenance of my dependant under s 52(n)`
    `a dealing with property held jointly with my administrator, or a loan or guarantee for it`

DECLARE `Whether my administrator's transaction is allowed` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: there is no conflict, so s 57 does not reach it`
    `allowed: s 57(1) does not apply to it (s 57(2))`
    `allowed: VCAT authorised it at or before the time (s 58(1))`
    `prohibited, but VCAT has validated it, so it is valid from the start (s 58(2), (3))`
    `prohibited (s 57(1))`

GIVEN `there is or may be a conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception` IS A `Conflict exception`
      `VCAT authorised it at or before the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT has validated it since` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether my administrator's transaction is allowed`
`ss 57, 58 -- whether my administrator's transaction is allowed` `there is or may be a conflict` `the exception` `VCAT authorised it at or before the time` `VCAT has validated it since` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `there is or may be a conflict`
            THEN `not covered: there is no conflict, so s 57 does not reach it` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF NOT (`the exception` EQUALS `no exception`)
            THEN `allowed: s 57(1) does not apply to it (s 57(2))`
        IF `VCAT authorised it at or before the time`
            THEN `allowed: VCAT authorised it at or before the time (s 58(1))`
        IF `VCAT has validated it since`
            THEN `prohibited, but VCAT has validated it, so it is valid from the start (s 58(2), (3))`
        OTHERWISE `prohibited (s 57(1))`

-- s 75(1): "Without an order of VCAT or the written consent of the administrator, to the extent that a financial matter
-- ... is subject to an administration order, the represented person is taken not to have decision-making capacity in
-- relation to (a) dealing with, transferring, alienating or charging [his or her] money or other property ...; or (b)
-- becoming liable under a contract." (2): "Any dealing, transfer, alienation or charge by a represented person in
-- relation to a financial matter that is subject to an administration order is void", recoverable by the
-- administrator. (3): not invalid if "made for adequate consideration" and the other person "proves that the other
-- person acted in good faith and did not know or could not reasonably have known" of the order. (4): accepting payment
-- of a debt is a dealing. Fork F11 (finding 5): the VCAT-order-or-consent words of (1) are read into (2).
DECLARE `Whether my own dealing is void` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: s 75 reaches only a financial matter that is subject to my administration order`
    `not void under s 75: VCAT ordered it or my administrator consented in writing (s 75(1))`
    `not void: the other person gave adequate consideration and proved good faith without knowledge (s 75(3))`
    `void: my administrator can recover the money or property (s 75(2))`

GIVEN `the matter is subject to my administration order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT ordered it or my administrator consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person gave adequate consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person proves good faith and that they did not and could not reasonably know` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether my own dealing is void`
`s 75 -- whether my own dealing is void` `the matter is subject to my administration order` `VCAT ordered it or my administrator consented in writing` `the other person gave adequate consideration` `the other person proves good faith and that they did not and could not reasonably know` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the matter is subject to my administration order`
            THEN `not covered: s 75 reaches only a financial matter that is subject to my administration order` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF `VCAT ordered it or my administrator consented in writing`
            THEN `not void under s 75: VCAT ordered it or my administrator consented in writing (s 75(1))`
        IF `the other person gave adequate consideration` AND `the other person proves good faith and that they did not and could not reasonably know`
            THEN `not void: the other person gave adequate consideration and proved good faith without knowledge (s 75(3))`
        OTHERWISE `void: my administrator can recover the money or property (s 75(2))`

-- s 177(4): "Unless otherwise agreed by each person appointed ... or unless otherwise directed by VCAT (a) a decision of
-- a guardian prevails over a decision of an administrator, to the extent of any inconsistency; and (b) subject to
-- subsection (5), an administrator must take any necessary steps to ensure that a guardian's decision may be
-- implemented." (5): if the administrator "reasonably believes" that doing so "is likely to deplete seriously the
-- represented person's estate", the administrator need not, and "must seek advice from VCAT".
DECLARE `Whose decision prevails` IS ONE OF
    `as they agreed, or as VCAT directed (s 177(4))`
    `my guardian's decision prevails, and my administrator must take the steps to implement it (s 177(4))`
    `my guardian's decision prevails, but my administrator need not implement it and must seek VCAT's advice (s 177(5))`

GIVEN `they agreed otherwise or VCAT directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my administrator reasonably believes it would seriously deplete my estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whose decision prevails`
`s 177 -- whose decision prevails` `they agreed otherwise or VCAT directed otherwise` `my administrator reasonably believes it would seriously deplete my estate` MEANS
    IF `they agreed otherwise or VCAT directed otherwise`
    THEN `as they agreed, or as VCAT directed (s 177(4))`
    ELSE IF `my administrator reasonably believes it would seriously deplete my estate`
         THEN `my guardian's decision prevails, but my administrator need not implement it and must seek VCAT's advice (s 177(5))`
         ELSE `my guardian's decision prevails, and my administrator must take the steps to implement it (s 177(4))`

-- s 93(1): VCAT may give a supportive guardian or administrator power "to take any reasonable action or do anything
-- that is reasonably necessary to give effect to a supported decision, other than a decision about a significant
-- financial transaction". (2): "significant financial transaction includes (a) making an investment ... or continuing
-- an investment ...; (b) undertaking any real estate transaction ..., excluding entering into a residential tenancy for
-- a premises in which the supported person lives or intends to live; (c) dealing with land ...; (d) ... use of the
-- supported person's property as security ...; (e) buying and selling substantial personal property". (3): (a) "does
-- not include investing or continuing an investment of an amount of $10 000 or less in total in one or more
-- interest-bearing accounts of an ADI." "Includes" leaves the list open: another kind of transaction is NOTHING
-- (fork F12: the residential tenancy taken as not significant).
DECLARE `Kind of transaction` IS ONE OF
    `investing in interest-bearing accounts with a bank or other ADI`
    `another investment, or continuing one`
    `entering into a residential tenancy of my home`
    `another real estate transaction or a dealing with land`
    `using my property as security`
    `buying or selling substantial personal property`
    `another kind of decision`

GIVEN `the order gives the s 93 power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction` IS A `Kind of transaction`
      `the total amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93 -- my supportive guardian or administrator may give effect to my decision` `the order gives the s 93 power` `the transaction` `the total amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order gives the s 93 power`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: no s 93 power specified (s 90(1)(d))
        IF `the transaction` EQUALS `investing in interest-bearing accounts with a bank or other ADI`
            THEN JUST (`the total amount` AT MOST 10000)
        IF `the transaction` EQUALS `entering into a residential tenancy of my home`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the transaction` EQUALS `another kind of decision`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: "includes" leaves open whether it is significant
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 3 Divisions 7 and 8 -- money, accounts, fees and the end of the order`

-- s 61(2): "Unless VCAT otherwise directs, on, or as soon as practicable after, the anniversary in each year of the
-- appointment of the administrator, the administrator must lodge with VCAT an account of the dealings and transactions
-- ... during the previous 12 months." The answer is the next anniversary on or after the day asked.
GIVEN `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE
      `VCAT has directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 61(2) -- when my administrator's next yearly account is due` `the day of the appointment` `VCAT has directed otherwise` `today` MEANS
    IF `VCAT has directed otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: VCAT's direction governs (s 61(2), (3))
    ELSE IF `the years so far` AT LEAST 1 AND (DATE_SERIAL (`the date` `the years so far` `years after` `the day of the appointment`) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `today`)
         THEN JUST `today`
         ELSE JUST (`the date` (`the years so far` PLUS 1) `years after` `the day of the appointment`)
    WHERE
        `the years so far` MEANS `the whole years from` `the day of the appointment` `to` `today`

-- s 61(6): "VCAT must not make an order disallowing an item ... if VCAT is satisfied that the administrator acted in
-- good faith and with reasonable care". (7): "If VCAT makes an order disallowing an item ..., the administrator is liable
-- for the amount of the item disallowed." (5)(b): the examiner or auditor may recommend the disallowance.
GIVEN `the auditor recommended disallowing the item` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied my administrator acted in good faith and with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT has ordered the item disallowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the item` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 61(6), (7) -- what my administrator must make good for a disallowed item` `the auditor recommended disallowing the item` `VCAT is satisfied my administrator acted in good faith and with reasonable care` `VCAT has ordered the item disallowed` `the amount of the item` MEANS
    IF `the auditor recommended disallowing the item` AND `VCAT has ordered the item disallowed` AND (NOT `VCAT is satisfied my administrator acted in good faith and with reasonable care`)
    THEN `the amount of the item`
    ELSE 0

-- s 175(1): an administrator "(other than a person who carries on a business of, or including, the administration of
-- estates) is not entitled to receive any fee, remuneration or other reward from the estate ... unless VCAT otherwise
-- specifies in the administration order". (2): a professional's remuneration "must be (a) in accordance with a scale
-- ... fixed by rules made under the VCAT Act; or (b) as determined by VCAT." (3): VCAT's determination for a licensed
-- trustee company "must not exceed the limit on fees ... under Chapter 5D of the Corporations Act". s 95: "A supportive
-- guardian or supportive administrator is not entitled to receive any remuneration". The scale and the Chapter 5D
-- limit are not deposited.
DECLARE `Who my administrator is` IS ONE OF
    `a supportive guardian or supportive administrator`
    `a licensed trustee company`
    `another person who carries on a business of administering estates`
    `anyone else, for example a family member`

DECLARE `What my administrator may charge` IS ONE OF
    `nothing at all (s 95)`
    `nothing from my estate (s 175(1))`
    `only what VCAT specified in the order (s 175(1))`
    `remuneration on the scale in the VCAT rules, or as VCAT determines (s 175(2))`
    `remuneration on the scale in the VCAT rules, or as VCAT determines but within the Chapter 5D limit (s 175(2), (3))`

GIVEN `the administrator` IS A `Who my administrator is`
      `VCAT specified remuneration in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What my administrator may charge`
`ss 95, 175 -- what my administrator may charge` `the administrator` `VCAT specified remuneration in the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the administrator` EQUALS `a supportive guardian or supportive administrator`
            THEN `nothing at all (s 95)`
        IF `the administrator` EQUALS `a licensed trustee company`
            THEN `remuneration on the scale in the VCAT rules, or as VCAT determines but within the Chapter 5D limit (s 175(2), (3))`
        IF `the administrator` EQUALS `another person who carries on a business of administering estates`
            THEN `remuneration on the scale in the VCAT rules, or as VCAT determines (s 175(2))`
        IF `VCAT specified remuneration in the order`
            THEN `only what VCAT specified in the order (s 175(1))`
        OTHERWISE `nothing from my estate (s 175(1))`

-- s 71(1): when the administrator "receives a notice under section 69 or is otherwise advised that a person has ceased
-- to be a represented person or has died", the administrator must pay to the person or the personal representative "all
-- money standing to the person's credit with the administrator" and deliver the property. (2): this "is subject to the
-- satisfaction of any amount due to the administrator and all costs, expenses and liabilities incurred". Not ended:
-- NOTHING.
GIVEN `the order has ended and my administrator knows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money standing to my credit` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts due to my administrator for costs, expenses and liabilities` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 71 -- the money my administrator must pay over` `the order has ended and my administrator knows` `the money standing to my credit` `the amounts due to my administrator for costs, expenses and liabilities` MEANS
    IF NOT `the order has ended and my administrator knows`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 71 applies when the order has ended
    ELSE IF `the money standing to my credit` GREATER THAN `the amounts due to my administrator for costs, expenses and liabilities`
         THEN JUST (`the money standing to my credit` MINUS `the amounts due to my administrator for costs, expenses and liabilities`)
         ELSE JUST 0

-- s 72: "Subject to an order under section 73, a person who has ceased to be a represented person (or the personal
-- representative ...) (a) may examine and inspect ... all books, accounts, notices and other documents in the custody of
-- the administrator ...; and (b) must be provided with" copies and reasonable information. s 73: VCAT may order a
-- document withheld. While I am still represented: NOTHING.
GIVEN `I have ceased to be a represented person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT has ordered the document withheld from me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 72, 73 -- I may inspect my former administrator's records` `I have ceased to be a represented person` `VCAT has ordered the document withheld from me` MEANS
    IF NOT `I have ceased to be a represented person`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 72 is for a former represented person
    ELSE IF `VCAT has ordered the document withheld from me`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 74(1): "After public notice, an administrator may sell any personal effect of a former represented person that
-- (a) is in the administrator's possession; and (b) is not claimed within 2 years after the date on which the person
-- ceased to be a represented person." (2): the proceeds go into the Consolidated Fund. The 2 years end on the second
-- anniversary; a sale is possible from the next day. A period the text fixes: before it ends, JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the day I ceased to be a represented person` IS A DATE
      `I have claimed the effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `public notice has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 74 -- my former administrator may sell my unclaimed personal effect` `the day I ceased to be a represented person` `I have claimed the effect` `public notice has been given` `today` MEANS
    (NOT `I have claimed the effect`)
    AND `public notice has been given`
    AND DATE_SERIAL `today` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the date` 2 `years after` `the day I ceased to be a represented person`)

§§ `Part 9 -- money a court orders paid to me (s 179)`

-- s 179(3): "If in any civil proceeding before a Court it is adjudged or ordered that money be paid to a person with a
-- disability (whether or not that person is a party ...), the money (a) is to be paid into court; and (b) unless the
-- Court otherwise orders, is to be paid out to the administrator (if any) for that person or State Trustees." (8): "An
-- order of the Court under this section that money be paid out to an administrator (if any) for a person or State
-- Trustees has effect as if it were an administration order." (9): "Court means (a) the Supreme Court; or (b) the
-- County Court; or (c) the Magistrates' Court." A "means" definition and an "if" condition: outside them, s 179 does
-- not apply (JUST FALSE-kind constructor). "the administrator (if any) ... or State Trustees" is read as the
-- administrator where there is one, otherwise State Trustees (fork F13).
DECLARE `Which court` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court`
    `the County Court`
    `the Magistrates' Court`
    `another court or tribunal`

DECLARE `Where the money a court awards me goes` IS ONE OF
    `paid into court, then paid out to my administrator; the payment-out order acts as an administration order (s 179(3), (8))`
    `paid into court, then paid out to State Trustees; the payment-out order acts as an administration order (s 179(3), (8))`
    `paid into court, then dealt with as the court orders (s 179(3))`
    `s 179 does not apply: it reaches only money a Supreme, County or Magistrates' Court orders paid in a civil proceeding to a person with a disability`

GIVEN `the court` IS A `Which court`
      `it is a civil proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the impairment` IS A `Kind of impairment`
      `the court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have an administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where the money a court awards me goes`
`s 179(3) -- where the money a court awards me goes` `the court` `it is a civil proceeding` `the impairment` `the court has ordered otherwise` `I have an administrator` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court` EQUALS `another court or tribunal` OR (NOT `it is a civil proceeding`) OR (NOT (`s 3 -- I have a disability` `the impairment`))
            THEN `s 179 does not apply: it reaches only money a Supreme, County or Magistrates' Court orders paid in a civil proceeding to a person with a disability`
        IF `the court has ordered otherwise`
            THEN `paid into court, then dealt with as the court orders (s 179(3))`
        IF `I have an administrator`
            THEN `paid into court, then paid out to my administrator; the payment-out order acts as an administration order (s 179(3), (8))`
        OTHERWISE `paid into court, then paid out to State Trustees; the payment-out order acts as an administration order (s 179(3), (8))`

-- s 179(1): "If in any civil proceeding before a Court the Court considers that a party may be in need of a guardian,
-- a supportive guardian, an administrator or a supportive administrator, the Court may refer the issue to VCAT". (2):
-- the referral is treated as an application, the prothonotary or principal registrar being the applicant.
GIVEN `the court` IS A `Which court`
      `it is a civil proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers I may need a guardian or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(1) -- the court hearing my claim may refer my need for a guardian or administrator to VCAT` `the court` `it is a civil proceeding` `I am a party` `the court considers I may need a guardian or administrator` MEANS
    IF `the court` EQUALS `another court or tribunal` OR (NOT `it is a civil proceeding`) OR (NOT `I am a party`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 179(1) is silent outside these courts and proceedings
    ELSE JUST `the court considers I may need a guardian or administrator`

§§ `Part 9 -- compensation from my guardian or administrator (ss 181-186)`

-- s 181(1): "The Supreme Court or VCAT may order a guardian or administrator to compensate the represented person ...
-- for a loss caused by the guardian or administrator contravening this Act when acting as guardian or administrator."
-- (2): even if the guardian or administrator was convicted, (b) "the represented person ... has died, in which case
-- compensation is payable to the estate", or (c) the order has ended. s 182: the court or VCAT may relieve one who
-- "acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused" from "all or part" of the personal liability. s 186:
-- "No compensation is payable by the State".
DECLARE `Relief from liability` IS ONE OF `no relief`, `relieved of part`, `relieved of all`

DECLARE `Whether I can be compensated` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: s 181 reaches only a loss caused by my guardian or administrator contravening this Act while acting`
    `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order my guardian or administrator to compensate me (s 181)`
    `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order compensation, payable to my estate (s 181(2)(b))`
    `yes, but only for the part of the liability not relieved (ss 181, 182)`
    `no: the Supreme Court or VCAT has relieved my guardian or administrator of all of it (s 182)`

GIVEN `the loss was caused by a contravention of the Act while acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relief` IS A `Relief from liability`
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether I can be compensated`
`ss 181, 182 -- whether I can be compensated` `the loss was caused by a contravention of the Act while acting` `the relief` `I have died` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the loss was caused by a contravention of the Act while acting`
            THEN `not covered: s 181 reaches only a loss caused by my guardian or administrator contravening this Act while acting` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF `the relief` EQUALS `relieved of all`
            THEN `no: the Supreme Court or VCAT has relieved my guardian or administrator of all of it (s 182)`
        IF `the relief` EQUALS `relieved of part`
            THEN `yes, but only for the part of the liability not relieved (ss 181, 182)`
        IF `I have died`
            THEN `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order compensation, payable to my estate (s 181(2)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order my guardian or administrator to compensate me (s 181)`

-- s 183: "The following persons may apply for an order for compensation under section 181 (a) the represented person
-- or a person who has ceased to be a represented person; (b) a former missing person; (c) the personal representative
-- of a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b); (d) an executor or administrator ... of the represented person's ...
-- estate; (e) the Public Advocate; (f) the nearest relative ...; (g) any other person the Supreme Court or VCAT
-- determines to have a special interest". A list not closed with "only": anyone else, NOTHING.
DECLARE `Who is applying for compensation` IS ONE OF
    `me, as a represented or former represented person`
    `my personal representative`
    `the executor or administrator of my estate`
    `the Public Advocate`
    `my nearest relative`
    `someone the Supreme Court or VCAT determines has a special interest in my affairs`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A `Who is applying for compensation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 -- this person may apply for compensation for me` `the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the applicant` EQUALS `someone else`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 183's list is not closed with "only"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 184: the last day, from the first death (or the extension). Neither death: s 184 sets no time.
GIVEN `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I died` IS A DATE
      `my guardian or administrator has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 184(1) -- the day of the first death` `I have died` `the day I died` `my guardian or administrator has died` `the day they died` MEANS
    IF `I have died` AND `my guardian or administrator has died`
    THEN IF `the day` `the day I died` `is on or before` `the day they died` THEN JUST `the day I died` ELSE JUST `the day they died`
    ELSE IF `I have died`
         THEN JUST `the day I died`
         ELSE IF `my guardian or administrator has died`
              THEN JUST `the day they died`
              ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the first death` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the time has been extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 184 -- the last day to apply for compensation from` `the first death` `the time has been extended` `the extended last day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the first death`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 184 sets no time limit while neither has died
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF `the time has been extended`
        THEN JUST `the extended last day`
        ELSE JUST (`the date` 6 `months after` d)

GIVEN `the first death` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the time has been extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`s 184 -- where my compensation application stands` `the first death` `the time has been extended` `the extended last day` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the first death`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no time limit under this provision`
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        `where the step stands under` (`s 184 -- apply for compensation within the time` (`the days from` d `to` `the last day`)) `me, or the person applying for me` `apply for an order for compensation` d `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today`
        WHERE
            `the last day` MEANS
                IF `the time has been extended`
                THEN `the extended last day`
                ELSE `the date` 6 `months after` d

§§ `Part 9 -- offences against me (ss 188-192)`

-- ss 188-192: a guardian, administrator, supportive guardian or supportive administrator "must not dishonestly use the
-- ... order to obtain financial advantage for [themself] or another person" ((1)) or "to cause loss to the represented
-- [supported] person or another person" ((2)). Penalty: "Level 6 imprisonment (5 years maximum) or 600 penalty units or
-- both"; for an administrator (s 189) "In the case of a body corporate, 2300 penalty units". s 192 gives a penalty
-- only "In the case of a natural person" (finding 6). Penalty units are not converted: the Monetary Units Act 2004 is
-- not deposited.
DECLARE `Who used the order dishonestly` IS ONE OF
    `my guardian`
    `my administrator`
    `my supportive guardian`
    `my supportive administrator`

DECLARE `Maximum penalty` HAS
    `penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the offender` IS A `Who used the order dishonestly`
      `the offender is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum penalty`
`ss 188-192 -- the maximum penalty for using the order dishonestly against me` `the offender` `the offender is a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the offender is a body corporate`
    THEN IF `the offender` EQUALS `my administrator`
         THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 2300, `years of imprisonment` IS 0)
         ELSE IF `the offender` EQUALS `my supportive administrator`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 192 sets a penalty only for a natural person
              ELSE JUST (`Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 600, `years of imprisonment` IS 5)
    ELSE JUST (`Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 600, `years of imprisonment` IS 5)
